2. What the ladder never collected: the registered Richardson band

   REGISTRATION-CONVERGED.md, verbatim: with L_k the ladder value at rung k,
   g = L_K - L_{K-1} and r = g / (L_{K-1} - L_{K-2}), the band is
   [L_K, L_K + g r / (1 - r)] for 0 < r < 1, and undefined otherwise, in which
   case the raw value and the last gain are reported alone. It is ONE-SIDED
   AND UPWARD: the converged reach can lie above L_K by up to the residual,
   and nothing here bounds it from below. r is read off the top three rungs
   only -- it is not a decay rate fitted across the ladder, which would be a
   different and much narrower band on a ladder that stalls at the top.

   The band is what gets published wherever 'accept' reads FAIL, i.e. wherever the
   last doubling of this ladder (6400 -> 12800) still gains more than 0.5 %; the
   registration fixes that acceptance at rung 12800 against rung 6400.

   n       L_K          g    g/L_K       r   residual  band top  accept
   8    0.6909   0.000000   0.000%       -          -         -    pass   the previous gain is zero; r undefined, no band
  10    0.5106   0.000000   0.000%   0.001   0.000000    0.5106    pass
  12    0.3534   0.000000   0.000%   0.000   0.000000    0.3534    pass
